{"chunk_id": "de5b9fb8720c", "text": "Arjuna reveals to Prince Uttara that his year-long disguise as the eunuch Brihannala was a vow taken to honor his elder brother\u2019s command and has now ended. Relieved that his suspicions were correct, Uttara eagerly offers to serve as Arjuna\u2019s charioteer and proudly describes the war chariot and its powerful horses. Arjuna then prepares for battle: he dons warrior gear, recalls his celestial weapons, and strings the mighty Gandiva bow, whose thunderous twang shakes the earth and alerts the Kauravas that Arjuna has returned. Though frightened by the ominous sounds and supernatural signs, Uttara is reassured by Arjuna\u2019s confident recollection of past heroic battles against gods, demons, and kings. Raising his celestial ape-banner and blowing his terrible conch, Arjuna sets out to face the Kaurava army, steadying the terrified Uttara and reminding him of his Kshatriya duty.\nArjuna reveals himself, prepares for battle with divine weapons and banner, reassures the frightened Uttara, and sets out to face the Kaurava army.\nThemes: heroic revelation, divine weapons, courage vs fear, war preparation, divine signs", "vector": [0.009364589117467403, -0.023916130885481834, -0.008107955567538738, 0.006192927714437246, 0.009471536614000797, 0.014224015176296234, -0.0364423543214798, -0.01479885820299387, -0.027752870693802834, -0.01380959339439869, 0.009344535879790783, 0.012492802925407887, -0.012071697041392326, -0.0007360994932241738, 0.0006888921489007771, 0.00842879805713892, 0.04352762550115585, 0.007172165438532829, 0.013562277890741825, -0.012954013422131538, 0.0036395564675331116, -0.013074330054223537, -0.007305849809199572, 0.017913702875375748, -0.009919378906488419, 0.014745384454727173, 0.011142591014504433, -0.028020240366458893, 0.0016743965679779649, -0.008422113955020905, -0.016817491501569748, 0.0013769487850368023, -0.0038835303857922554, -0.0063065593130886555, -0.02876887284219265, 0.00470903143286705, 0.